    "description": "<p>Assume the scalar isoperimetric profile and equality classification for the cubic flat three-torus stated in the paper. We determine the sharp summed-perimeter cost of nesting a ball-volume region inside a slightly thinned tube-volume or slab-volume region, minimizing over all finite-perimeter pairs. For ball–tube contact the minimum is asymptotic to K(R) epsilon squared, where K(R) = 4 pi R / (R + 4 G_R) and G_R = R squared - (R/2) cot(1/(2R)), for 2/9 &lt; R &lt; 1/pi. For ball–slab contact it is asymptotic to 2 pi epsilon squared / |log epsilon|, for 1/(2 pi) &lt; R &lt; 1/3. A common volume-correction flow gives scalar quasiminimality of exact paired minimizers. The sharp constants then follow from the coupled quadratic problem and logarithmic capacity at the two polar contacts.</p>",
    "references": [
      {
        "reference": "E. Acerbi, N. Fusco, and M. Morini, Minimality via second variation for a nonlocal isoperimetric problem, Comm. Math. Phys. 322 (2013), 515–557. doi:10.1007/s00220-013-1733-y."
      },
      {
        "reference": "M.-D. Lacasse, G. S. Grest, and D. Levine, Deformation of small compressed droplets, arXiv:mtrl-th/9603005, 1996."
      },
      {
        "reference": "C. Lv, Effects of geometric confinement on a droplet between two parallel planes, arXiv:1704.05830, 2017."
      },
      {
        "reference": "D. C. Morse and T. A. Witten, Droplet elasticity in weakly compressed emulsions, Europhysics Letters 22 (1993), 549–555. doi:10.1209/0295-5075/22/7/012."
      },
      {
        "reference": "G. Ginot, R. Höhler, S. Mariot, A. Kraynik, and W. Drenckhan, Juggling bubbles in square capillaries: an experimental proof of non-pairwise bubble interactions, Soft Matter (2019). doi:10.1039/C8SM02477D."
      },
      {
        "reference": "S. Alama, L. Bronsard, X. Lu, and C. Wang, Core shells and double bubbles in a weighted nonlocal isoperimetric problem, arXiv:2212.06381v4."
      },
      {
        "reference": "OpenAI, The isoperimetric conjecture for the cubic flat three-torus, September 24, 2026. Repository revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb. Pinned manuscript, Theorem 1.1."
      }
    ]
  },
